{
  "summary": "This experiment directly combined multiprofile+avgpool aggregation with multimodal (ResNet-50, concat) fusion under scVI_n200 to test whether the previously observed multiprofile gain (~13% over singleprofile RNA-only) and the multimodal gain (~1.6% over RNA-only) are additive. The validation accuracy of 0.632 (F1 0.607) falls below the RNA-only multiprofile result (0.650, F1 0.628) and well below the simple additive prediction (~0.666), indicating the two gains are not additive; the multimodal configuration with multiprofile aggregation underperforms the RNA-only multiprofile baseline by ~1.9%. The multiprofile benefit is still present in the multimodal setting (0.632 vs. 0.536 for singleprofile multimodal scVI), but adding the image modality on top of multiprofile+avgpool does not yield the expected additional gain. It remains uncertain whether the slight underperformance relative to RNA-only multiprofile reflects noise introduced by the image features, an interaction between concat fusion and avgpool, or other factors, and whether alternative fusion or aggregation strategies could restore or exceed the RNA-only multiprofile performance."
}

